# Android Auto host constraints

Full reference: [`docs/android-auto.md`](../../docs/android-auto.md). Official: [template restrictions](https://developer.android.com/training/cars/apps/library/template-restrictions).

## Required patterns (every Screen)

- Wrap `onGetTemplate()` in `safeCarTemplate(carContext, logTag, templateName) { … }` (`CarTemplateSafe.kt`).
- Never hardcode item limits — use `ConstraintManager.getContentLimit(type)` (car API 6+, wrap in try/catch with the minimum as fallback): `LIST`=6, `GRID`=6, `PLACE_LIST`=6, `PANE`=4, `ROUTE_LIST`=3.
- `onGetTemplate()` runs on the main thread — do async work in `init`/`onStart` and `invalidate()` when ready (never block).
- Category `POI`: allowed templates are `PlaceListMap`, `MapWithContent`, `List`, `Grid`, `Pane`, `Message`, `LongMessage`, `Search`, `SignIn`, `Tab` — **no** `NavigationTemplate`.
- Rows that push a screen: `.setBrowsable(true)` + `setOnClickListener { screenManager.push(…) }`.
- Toggle/action rows (zoom, sort): **not** browsable.

## Screen stack & template quota (5 steps per task)

Official: [template restrictions — Template quota](https://developer.android.com/training/cars/apps/library/template-restrictions). Full Gaston guide: [`docs/android-auto.md`](../../docs/android-auto.md#screen-stack--template-quota-5-steps-per-task).

- Each **task** = max **5 template steps**; exceeding quota **closes the app** (host-side, not catchable).
- **Step** = host shows a template whose **type or main content** differs from the previous step. Each `screenManager.push()` to a new template usually +1.
- **Refresh** (no step): same `Screen` + same template type + same main content via `invalidate()` (sort toggle, load data on same list).
- **5th step must be terminal**: `PaneTemplate`, `MessageTemplate`, `LongMessageTemplate`, `SignInTemplate`, `MediaPlaybackTemplate`, or `NavigationTemplate` (Gaston POI: use `LongMessageTemplate` / `PaneTemplate` / `MessageTemplate` — no `NavigationTemplate`).
- **Back restores quota**; resumed screen must return the **same template type** it last showed.
- **POI has no navigation reset** — all flows must fit in 5 steps without `NavigationTemplate`.
- Before adding `push()`: count steps from root (map/dashboard = 1). Flatten deep settings/filter chains; use `TabTemplate` or `invalidate()` instead of extra screens.
- Debug: DHU template-step overlay; `adb logcat -s CarApp:V`.
- Gaston pattern: `PlaceListMapStationDetailScreen` pushed for BACK nav (not in-place detail on browsable rows).

## Message content

| Template | Use for | Body limit |
|----------|---------|------------|
| `MessageTemplate` | Short status/errors | **~500 chars** — always `.take(500)` |
| `LongMessageTemplate` | Station detail, about, scrollable text | **~5000 chars** — `.take(5000)` |

- Use **plain `String`** bodies — avoid `SpannableString` / style spans (strict hosts reject them).
- `LongMessageTemplate`: `setTitle` + `setHeaderAction(BACK)` + `addAction` for primary actions (not `Header.addEndHeaderAction`).
- `LongMessageTemplate` body actions (`addAction`) **must** use `ParkedOnlyOnClickListener.create { … }` — a plain `setOnClickListener` throws `IllegalArgumentException` at build time and the host rejects the screen.
- `MessageTemplate`: max **2** `addAction()`; optional icon.

## Row rules

- **Forbidden**: `Row.IMAGE_TYPE_LARGE` + `Metadata.setPlace()` on same row → use `IMAGE_TYPE_SMALL`.
- `PlaceListMapTemplate` rows: must include `Metadata.setPlace(...)` for map pins; use `includePlace = true` in `AutoPoiUiHelper.buildPoiRow`.
- `MapWithContentTemplate` list rows: `includePlace = false` (app draws map); row uses `setImage`.
- Max **2** `addText()` per row.
- Include `DistanceSpan` on list rows when distance is shown (`AutoPoiUiHelper` pattern).

## ListTemplate / PlaceListMapTemplate

- `setLoading(true)` and item list are **mutually exclusive**.
- Header: `setStartHeaderAction(BACK)` or `APP_ICON` (root).
- End header actions: max 2 (prefer 1 on strict hosts).

## ActionStrip

| Template | Max actions |
|----------|-------------|
| List, Grid, Pane, Message, SignIn… | **2** |
| MapWithContent, PlaceListMap, Navigation | **4** |

- Map templates: **icon required** on every action (title-only rejected).
- Max **1 label button** (title visible) per strip; rest icon-only.
- `Action.BACK` / `Action.APP_ICON` → header only, never in ActionStrip.
- Gaston map screens: keep ActionStrip minimal (settings ± errors); put zoom/recenter on nested `Header` end actions.

## MapWithContentTemplate (CustomMapPoiScreen, MapLibrePoiScreen)

- Permissions: `MAP_TEMPLATES` + `ACCESS_SURFACE`; `minCarApiLevel` **7**.
- Content: `ListTemplate` | `GridTemplate` | `PaneTemplate` | `MessageTemplate` only.
- Register `SurfaceCallback` in `onStart`, stop renderer in `onStop`.

## PlaceListMapTemplate (NativeMapPoiScreen)

- Host-rendered map — app cannot control bearing/zoom. Use `CustomMapPoiScreen` for orientation toggle.
- Set anchor `Place` for user location. Loading vs item list mutually exclusive.

## GridTemplate

- Items: cap at `CONTENT_LIMIT_TYPE_GRID` (min 6). Each `GridItem` needs a title + image (`IMAGE_TYPE_LARGE`/`IMAGE_TYPE_ICON`); no `Place` metadata.
- `setLoading(true)` and item list mutually exclusive.

## PaneTemplate

- Rows: cap at `CONTENT_LIMIT_TYPE_PANE` (min 4); rows **not** browsable. Pane actions: max **2** (one may be `FLAG_PRIMARY`).
- Valid as a terminal (last-step) template.

## TabTemplate

- Nested `ListTemplate` inside `TabContents` must **not** have header or title.

## POI category (Gaston)

- Category: `androidx.car.app.category.POI` — no `NavigationTemplate`, no `AppManager.showAlert()`.
- Alerts: phone notifications + `CarAppExtender` / HUN (see `docs/android-auto.md`).

## Common runtime failures

1. Long text in `MessageTemplate` → `LongMessageTemplate`
2. Row image + Place metadata → `IMAGE_TYPE_SMALL` or split image vs place
3. >6 list rows without `ConstraintManager` → `.take(listLimit)`
4. Map ActionStrip title-only → add icon
5. Screen push row missing `setBrowsable(true)`
6. Template quota >5 pushes → flatten navigation or use refresh
7. Host rejection after `onGetTemplate()` returns → not catchable; check `adb logcat -s CarApp`
8. `LongMessageTemplate` `addAction` with plain `setOnClickListener` → use `ParkedOnlyOnClickListener.create { … }`

